      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/SamueleMoscatelli/pulse",
          "name": "pulse",
          "rules": [
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# AI-COG-006 — Weak routing description\n\n**Severity:** Medium · **Category:** Cognitive · **Applies to:** skills, agents · **Inline-suppressible:** yes\n\n## Why it matters\nThe model decides whether to load a skill or delegate to an agent from its `description` alone. A description that is too short, never says when to use it, or speaks as \"I\" leads to missed or wrong invocations.\n\n## What triggers it\nOne finding at the `description` line when any of these holds (the message lists which):\n- Fewer than 20 words.\n- No trigger cue: `use`/`used` followed within 4 words by `when`, `whenever`, `for` or `if` (\"Use this agent when …\"), `when the user`, or a word starting with `trigger`, `invok` or `proactive`.\n- First person: `I`, `I'm`, `I'll`, `I've`, `I'd` outside quotes or code spans (quoted user speech such as `\"I need a review\"` is fine).\n\nA missing or empty description is AI-STR-001's, not this rule's.\n\n## Noncompliant\n```markdown\n---\nname: pdf-tools\ndescription: I extract text from PDF files.\n---\n```\n\n## Compliant\n```markdown\n---\nname: pdf-tools\ndescription: Extract text, tables and form fields from PDF files and merge or split documents. Use when the user asks to read, fill or combine PDFs.\n---\n```\n\n## Options\nNone.\n\n## Suppressing\n`<!-- pulse-ignore AI-COG-006 -- reason -->` (Markdown) or a `[[ignore]]` entry in `pulse.toml`.\n",
                "text": "Say what it does and when to use it, in the third person: \"Use when the user …\"."
              },
              "id": "AI-COG-006",
              "name": "Weak routing description",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "cognitive"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A skill or agent description is too short, lacks a trigger cue, or is in first person."
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "# AI-STR-002 — Invalid file content\n\n**Severity:** High (Info for skipped files) · **Category:** Structure · **Applies to:** all assets · **Inline-suppressible:** yes\n\n## Why it matters\nAgents read these files literally. A JSON syntax error can make a tool ignore the whole MCP config or settings file without any warning. Broken YAML frontmatter can drop a skill's `description`, so it never triggers. Pulse can't analyze what it can't parse, so the other rules see less of the file too.\n\n## What triggers it\n- Bytes that are not valid UTF-8 (Pulse decodes them as U+FFFD and keeps going).\n- JSON/JSONC syntax errors in MCP configs, settings, hooks and tool definitions.\n- Wrong shape for the kind, e.g. `mcpServers` is not an object or `permissions.allow` is not an array of strings.\n- YAML frontmatter that does not parse into a mapping.\n- Files over `scan.max_file_bytes`, or files that can't be read: reported at Info as \"skipped\", not analyzed.\n\n## Noncompliant\n```json\n{ \"mcpServers\": [\"github\"] }\n```\n\n## Compliant\n```json\n{ \"mcpServers\": { \"github\": { \"command\": \"npx\", \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-github@1.0.0\"] } } }\n```\n\n## Options\nNone.\n\n## Suppressing\n`<!-- pulse-ignore AI-STR-002 -- reason -->` (Markdown) or a `[[ignore]]` entry in `pulse.toml`.\n",
                "text": "Fix the syntax or shape so the agent (and Pulse) can read the whole file."
              },
              "id": "AI-STR-002",
              "name": "Invalid file content",
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "structure"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "File is not valid UTF-8, JSON, YAML frontmatter, or has the wrong shape for its kind."
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "1.0.0"
        }
      }
    }
